881-85f2-52b3-8728-2b2e2b235db9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3t^2+2}{t^3+2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352539/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "334c5d00-be75-5ac0-9a97-bcbe80a1f88f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352539/field-1/be150930d76d2bceed847ae28b9b1c25444634413e5d7c1ade5dfb31a04f55ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-352539/field-1/be150930d76d2bceed847ae28b9b1c25444634413e5d7c1ade5dfb31a04f55ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352539" :question/id #uuid "d3593e3a-62f3-5ba1-ba98-5a7176a17945" :question/math-academy-id "q-352539" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3}+2t),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9-{t}^{2})⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$\n\n$v=⟨${{field-1}}$,\\,-\\frac{2t}{9-{t}^{2}}\\,⟩$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3}+2t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9-{t}^{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3{t}^{2}+2}{{t}^{3}+2t},-\\frac{2t}{9-{t}^{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352539/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dccdc3ad-6acb-57ae-83ef-95ffedfbff2f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352539"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352536/field-1/af4e9d1b2391640bcaff594d809abbe2ec30aaad4a4cd38854278868d942fcb5" :answer/id #uuid "77b47ecd-3c34-5f7b-acf0-198326c89cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6t}{3t^2+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352536/field-1/81834f3b629a778af633bcfaab6110106