e4d7c591e704ae6d8fd379ae80ad85c00899fe41634de7067e08f8b" "q-121722/selection/212e64c1f1f03142f43b88f0174f3b3b356c4d447424d1f454d31ee8bd07bac8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121722" :question/id #uuid "21d59417-64de-5660-afc1-3936a54352ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-121722" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨1-5t,{e}^{2t}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-5t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,2{e}^{2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨-5,2{e}^{2(1)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,2{e}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-121722/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352570/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "8c132b5e-7bda-554f-bc5b-a5c02cc0c708" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352570/field-1/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "7edc0ef2-3374-5396-bf68-fe6d96efaf91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352570/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "16d9c637-816b-5e0f-aadd-9066f3e555aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352570/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-352570/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-352570/field-1/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352570/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "6c292866-73c9-5d3b-a563-fa23a15c6a9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352570/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "bce0b200-17e2-503f-95eb-67ac0ce7ad5b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352570/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-352570/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352570" :question/id #uuid "6a005320-38e4-5c29-a628-b544e5ffac11" :question/math-academy-id "q-352570" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨5\\sqrt{1+8t},\\,(3+2t)^{3/2}⟩,\\,0<t<4.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(3)=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\sqrt{1+8t}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((3+2t)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1+8t)^{-1/2}\\cdot 8,\\frac{3}{2}(3+2t)^{1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{1+8t}},3\\sqrt{3+2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{1+8(3)}},3\\sqrt{3+2(3)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{25}},3\\sqrt{9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{20}{5},3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352570/field-1" "q-352570/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75290/selection/32d972b0218d037f8d10a69c9b28e710a359cfe2d29aba9739dcd20249d64e96" :answer/id #uuid "3fd6f126-ee0b-58dc-8cc4-6a3bb77cbc5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨4,\\,8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75290/selection/e461fb31eeec56f4110b406c7ea7dfc9d3c2fc610eaa1420f6e49ca8777c9ece" :answer/id #uuid "7759ed35-5b2e-5585-bf80-e5d8a0e8ebf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨2,\\,8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75290/selection/184f9caa07a9affd84002f0103c9a4e73dcba372fc90a7b7bee66fdc017607fb" :answer/id #uuid "418df1f8-c1b6-5814-93ab-50d1f6b8bf52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨1,\\,7⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75290/selection/d5fbb40c04bac3df16d58f684e247be7750dfe7f2f8df2379feab3349a0781fc" :answer/id #uuid "c224322a-eb76-5047-a8c8-09047a630b86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨2,\\,7⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75290/selection/e4e973f38969e6868c1d9b66b79740f70b8fc3cd8672907a3d8871885ad22e2c" :answer/id #uuid "688c6f84-12da-5c59-8a7b-1ecf2bfff4b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨1,\\,8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "20395fba-119a-5a5f-ac76-ddd929d57598" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75290/selection/e4e973f38969e6868c1d9b66b79740f70b8fc3cd8672907a3d8871885ad22e2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-75290/selection/32d972b0218d037f8d10a69c9b28e710a359cfe2d29aba9739dcd20249d64e96" "q-75290/selection/e461fb31eeec56f4110b406c7ea7dfc9d3c2fc610eaa1420f6e49ca8777c9ece" "q-75290/selection/184f9caa07a9affd84002f0103c9a4e73dcba372fc90a7b7bee66fdc017607fb" "q-75290/selection/d5fbb40c04bac3df16d58f684e247be7750dfe7f2f8df2379feab3349a0781fc" "q-75290/selection/e4e973f38969e6868c1d9b66b79740f70b8fc3cd8672907a3d8871885ad22e2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75290" :question/id #uuid "6f58a47e-55ad-5bda-ac53-f0cf87e9e705" :question/math-academy-id "q-75290" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4\\sqrt{1+t},(1+t)^{2}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{1+t}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((1+t)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(1+t)^{-1/2},2(1+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1+t}},2+2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1+3}},2+2(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{2},\\,2+6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121720/selection/861b488ed04a53d9e7570d508c90a2adbe307b2216c615521dc6f4f8c5584a84" :answer/id #uuid "8bac786a-850a-5142-a9d4-89c95623fd9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121720/selection/c07ac7bf5843dffe8692530efc3139aecd907cd644c9c25e533026e755faa457" :answer/id #uuid "7e06ad6f-b267-551b-ac40-9fb77d5b3081" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨-1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121720/selection/0e502ff2994ebf15d5ea1da60950de8076aad2008424212b16a3002d86d4855e" :answer/id #uuid "b3db8b19-d568-50d0-a489-5717e1bb7dc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨1,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121720/selection/7afa7eca60d0fe30e0f82f1588e41bbf7fc5c82188e34e2e96f62e6aebbe5b97" :answer/id #uuid "fec23b36-0478-5117-9ca8-0bc7ae7f0246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨-1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121720/selection/f1f6768ececb56f41006e2d1a05871ffb5f5baf9560a647759e193cf9d2e2acc" :answer/id #uuid "7ca0f76c-5c2a-580b-86a5-6460adef95ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121720/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47393157-bd26-51b5-95d4-a3633a396640" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121720/selection/861b488ed04a53d9e7570d508c90a2adbe307b2216c615521dc6f4f8c5584a84" :answer-field/choices ["q-121720/selection/861b488ed04a53d9e7570d508c90a2adbe307b2216c615521dc6f4f8c5584a84" "q-121720/selection/c07ac7bf5843dffe8692530efc3139aecd907cd644c9c25e533026e755faa457" "q-121720/selection/0e502ff2994ebf15d5ea1da60950de8076aad2008424212b16a3002d86d4855e" "q-121720/selection/7afa7eca60d0fe30e0f82f1588e41bbf7fc5c82188e34e2e96f62e6aebbe5b97" "q-121720/selection/f1f6768ececb56f41006e2d1a05871ffb5f5baf9560a647759e193cf9d2e2acc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121720" :question/id #uuid "741539b0-f482-543c-8cda-1da90dd97aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-121720" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121720/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121719/selection/a41d4dcd757e94a3b8c3501c938cd5b9170611fadbcc48141ac0f1e43b3b08a2" :answer/id #uuid "a2c8f43f-a984-54f6-a907-f85658be243c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨1,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121719/selection/fc71fff489661ff91c0806a0115d6769738cca0d208a37d72c2e263d40a264b2" :answer/id #uuid "1ecdcea4-4f24-5b43-8d28-0a7494ee797b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨1,\\frac{5}{4}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121719/selection/2247fefd10d983e89c61acfb75901f438b42cfd00642aaee1c30bbad67d2fd45" :answer/id #uuid "fb640a6d-7a76-5ec1-a798-704771be4a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨7,\\frac{5}{16}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121719/selection/2395cfbc44d2cdf1a5b15b9fa6e272e2acb51bedb63628a0c0a5dc795e4390ad" :answer/id #uuid "5ae625d0-7603-54d3-bbfe-7d20ed6b215f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨7,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121719/selection/29feb4f937f9f9b2c13ae12f6a1a31154f76e87009a1ce70f912ac48147af8f4" :answer/id #uuid "e823262b-d709-5dca-a52b-ab1a94ec509c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(3)=⟨1,\\frac{5}{16}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121719/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4053636-baf7-51ec-b9f5-03830a0a55f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121719/selection/29feb4f937f9f9b2c13ae12f6a1a31154f76e87009a1ce70f912ac48147af8f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-121719/selection/a41d4dcd757e94a3b8c3501c938cd5b9170611fadbcc48141ac0f1e43b3b08a2" "q-121719/selection/fc71fff489661ff91c0806a0115d6769738cca0d208a37d72c2e263d40a264b2" "q-121719/selection/2247fefd10d983e89c61acfb75901f438b42cfd00642aaee1c30bbad67d2fd45" "q-121719/selection/2395cfbc44d2cdf1a5b15b9fa6e272e2acb51bedb63628a0c0a5dc795e4390ad" "q-121719/selection/29feb4f937f9f9b2c13ae12f6a1a31154f76e87009a1ce70f912ac48147af8f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121719" :question/id #uuid "03870043-e61d-591f-9542-928769f96294" :question/math-academy-id "q-121719" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨t+4,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t+1)⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+4),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\frac{5}{5t+1}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨1,\\frac{5}{5(3)+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\frac{5}{16}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121719/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352588/field-1/42fcd1b5e1296194d4394bc7ef076f3352e45d83ec86bea5c243c8d2031e2d4f" :answer/id #uuid "d720b213-48a4-514d-bb6a-de868f54160f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352588/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "42b67214-0fe8-5675-94ac-cef6f791a1f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352588/field-1/42fcd1b5e1296194d4394bc7ef076f3352e45d83ec86bea5c243c8d2031e2d4f" :answer-field/choices ["q-352588/field-1/42fcd1b5e1296194d4394bc7ef076f3352e45d83ec86bea5c243c8d2031e2d4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352588" :question/id #uuid "edb7fca2-61e2-5800-a4c9-2d1de8e94995" :question/math-academy-id "q-352588" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{1+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=1$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352588/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75302/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "a06432fe-fa44-5a17-bc32-2d7362adabfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75302/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer/id #uuid "6749f6f8-90f6-5481-a85a-58d5822e6356" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75302/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "3cd015fc-178b-5c8f-876d-ea9bc050f144" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75302/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "5058623a-1137-569d-ac5c-32bf494eea2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75302/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "e71e3848-d37d-56a9-8db2-ba08016c2a8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75302/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d180a47c-8720-55e6-8def-33ab730913c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75302/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-75302/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-75302/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" "q-75302/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-75302/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-75302/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75302" :question/id #uuid "71df76b4-b01c-58e6-a008-71b6cfb97015" :question/math-academy-id "q-75302" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4(0),4(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75302/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352584/field-1/7716c3d072c6beb96c4429fc0151ff524c3a282e6b66458b3979dc4e3551257f" :answer/id #uuid "fc38d2dc-1527-56e3-96af-51823830504a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352584/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec00e37a-ad51-598d-b18a-2ef6678ae717" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352584/field-1/7716c3d072c6beb96c4429fc0151ff524c3a282e6b66458b3979dc4e3551257f" :answer-field/choices ["q-352584/field-1/7716c3d072c6beb96c4429fc0151ff524c3a282e6b66458b3979dc4e3551257f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352584" :question/id #uuid "b661ab3f-53c8-53bd-9aca-1b6a65f8f496" :question/math-academy-id "q-352584" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+2),\\,\\frac{4}{t}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=2$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+2)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t+2},\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨\\frac{1}{2+2},\\,-\\frac{4}{{2}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{4},\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352584/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352596/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "2027ea17-89db-5e33-aa05-0177b2f0450a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352596/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "364e4a22-93a9-5ccc-8699-62a04f227ce1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352596/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f449c06-653a-5e84-804c-c7eb77aa2bd9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352596/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-352596/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-352596/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352596" :question/id #uuid "def01361-ad83-523b-8ea1-25745a466c56" :question/math-academy-id "q-352596" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}t),\\,\\sqrt{t+2}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2.$\n\nThe speed at time $t=2$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t+2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}t),\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t+2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2+2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\frac{1}{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352596/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352572/field-1/bf1594b2b59f412ac8c1d70a1897a42a529be0f6bffa467dda288ace33ef2e85" :answer/id #uuid "4d5835d4-8696-554f-bb70-a2bda4ac2d94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{26}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352572/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e8ceebc-1b05-539e-91d2-8fbd23848387" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352572/field-1/bf1594b2b59f412ac8c1d70a1897a42a529be0f6bffa467dda288ace33ef2e85" :answer-field/choices ["q-352572/field-1/bf1594b2b59f412ac8c1d70a1897a42a529be0f6bffa467dda288ace33ef2e85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352572" :question/id #uuid "810e6c21-1003-5a47-b790-30b10392715b" :question/math-academy-id "q-352572" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2},\\,3t+2⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed  $|v|$ of the particle at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe speed at time $t=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨5(3),\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨15,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=3$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(3)| & =\\sqrt{{15}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{225+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{234} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{26}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352572/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352572"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/selection/5af4b542c90e395f5f4af499da66123a12579005cf0807c6a5587df7b0db3f99" :answer/id #uuid "cd023b9a-ef5b-5edf-b8dc-e77258dc8f06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" :answer/id #uuid "a97c7458-8a57-593f-b53b-0777e07d4888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer/id #uuid "08779a6f-b0b9-56ff-8814-a43c29ab9a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" :answer/id #uuid "9dc23d8d-070f-50b0-b07c-8adbf9c7ce5c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/selection/68b9609c73019519096d74c9eb72d7cf21e3a1157aa880ff36e5de58ba989cf7" :answer/id #uuid "1626e7f9-33d1-54f5-aa99-61752c0c4688" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1d504dc-d3ab-59bc-b706-2a6beff615f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121736/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" :answer-field/choices ["q-121736/selection/5af4b542c90e395f5f4af499da66123a12579005cf0807c6a5587df7b0db3f99" "q-121736/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" "q-121736/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" "q-121736/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" "q-121736/selection/68b9609c73019519096d74c9eb72d7cf21e3a1157aa880ff36e5de58ba989cf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736" :question/id #uuid "942f342e-d375-5134-864c-b37213f6cf64" :question/math-academy-id "q-121736" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-4t+8),{t}^{4}-\\frac{8}{3}{t}^{3}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-4t+8),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-\\frac{8}{3}{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t-4}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{2}(t-2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{2}(t-2)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=2, \\\\ 4{t}^{2}(t-2)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=2$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-121736/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31653/selection/68b9609c73019519096d74c9eb72d7cf21e3a1157aa880ff36e5de58ba989cf7" :answer/id #uuid "1d9f3411-f0d0-5426-963b-c243f89c9335" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31653/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" :answer/id #uuid "443bc0ba-ec31-5637-80e0-f8f036f72645" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31653/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer/id #uuid "c2503e2d-37ff-535a-9654-39638b24e106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31653/selection/2116b39709904c2e9d6e8528e9a76e091054e59cf88ed0d3c032ec988e82f266" :answer/id #uuid "9d405f24-ea34-58cd-9307-88b43953de92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31653/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea" :answer/id #uuid "391b90c8-0461-59f1-a74e-1d2b9bb3b81a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31653/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8d7bd5d-e198-549f-8d29-91bff585f890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31653/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer-field/choices ["q-31653/selection/68b9609c73019519096d74c9eb72d7cf21e3a1157aa880ff36e5de58ba989cf7" "q-31653/selection/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" "q-31653/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" "q-31653/selection/2116b39709904c2e9d6e8528e9a76e091054e59cf88ed0d3c032ec988e82f266" "q-31653/selection/24b44fba53578fd75922a19937c1240a9736e2dc7d7ad97ff6285932419cf4ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31653" :question/id #uuid "645e5a65-0546-5aaf-862f-784af9633470" :question/math-academy-id "q-31653" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1},\\,{t}^{3}-6{t}^{2}⟩,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-6{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({t}^{2}+1)^{-1/2}\\cdot 2t,3{t}^{2}-12t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}},3t(t-4)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}},3t(t-4)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0, \\\\ 3t(t-4)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=0$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the object is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-31653/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31653"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352729/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5eb323b7-2a9c-5e57-9d96-8d03a0fc8aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352729/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d7baf41-bc4f-55f5-add8-231725817a72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352729/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-352729/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352729" :question/id #uuid "407b9aae-8296-546a-aea3-e0d4a26f0781" :question/math-academy-id "q-352729" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨t-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary.\n\nThe particle is stationary at $t=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =0 \\\\ ⟨1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0, \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=0$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the object is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352729/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352729"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352732/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3a1b2b9f-00d2-53fa-925c-73024cdc4644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352732/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7463eb62-799a-59e0-9808-ba9cc58ef7f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352732/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-352732/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352732" :question/id #uuid "fea150a4-e472-5de1-95f5-af02e8f830f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-352732" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary.\n\nThe particle is stationary at $t=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =0 \\\\ ⟨1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0, \\\\ \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=0$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the object is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352732/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352732"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
